{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> The labor of Egypt — this too is for a sign, that Cyrus will plunder Egypt and they will be taken captive. And it is known that their route is through the land of Israel, for it lies between Elam and Egypt:" "<b>Men of stature.</b> The meaning is greatness, for every great man has measure, and likewise וחזקת והיית לאיש (1 Kings 2:2)." "<b>And they shall submit and say: Only in you, El.</b> And this was after the return of the exile:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:11.045449890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}